# Custom screen firmware (`re/custom/`)

Default stance: **do not change the firmware.** Almost every feature (pages,
weather, notifications, images, services) belongs in the laptop tool
(`rt100screen.py`). Only touch firmware files if the user asks for a firmware
change specifically, and even then never flash (see hardware-safety rule).

## Do not edit
- Any hard-coded address: `link.ld` origins/symbols, `hooks.S`, the `#define`s at the
  top of `custom.c` (stock routine and RAM addresses), and the constants in `build.py`
  (`FRAME_SITE*`, `LOOP_SITE`, `ZI_*`, `APP_*`, `BASE_SHA256`). These came from
  disassembly of firmware v506; a wrong value bricks the screen.
- The wire protocol (`PKT_*`, `OP_*` values, packet layout) without changing
  `screenproto.py` in the same change and keeping old opcodes working.

## Invariants `custom.c` must keep (if a change is approved)
- `custom_frame_hook` runs in the timer interrupt: no drawing, no loops over pixels,
  no waiting. It only copies the packet, handles `PKT_NOW`, and sets the reply.
- Unknown serial commands must still set `UNHANDLED = 1` (stock behaviour).
- Any loop that can take milliseconds calls `wdt_feed()` (watchdog reset otherwise).
- No libc, no initialised globals (`.data` must stay empty), no floating point.
- `QN` stays a power of two; state lives in the zero-initialised `st` struct so
  custom mode never survives a reboot.
- Code must end below `0x01020000`; `.bss` below `0x0002D000` (build asserts both).

## Required checks after any change under `re/custom/`
```bash
cd re/custom
../../.venv/bin/python build.py 2>&1 | rg -v "Forcing branch"
../../.venv/bin/python emu_custom.py   # must print ALL CHECKS PASSED
```
Then show the user `out/emu_*.png` and `out/patch.txt`, and stop. Flashing is the
user's decision, asked explicitly, every time.

Never weaken or delete a check in `build.py` or `emu_custom.py` to make it pass.
